\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S13}{\ignorespaces Hallmark labels of every response programme, by section, seed and programme (within a fit in order of variance; its share of $\mathbf  {w}$'s within-type variance, in $\%$, above). All $50$ sets were tested on every programme and Benjamini--Hochberg correction is applied within each programme. Rows: the sets significant on at least one programme, with the number of such programmes in parentheses. Cells: the AUC of the Mann--Whitney test of the set's absolute loadings against the rest of the expressed panel ($0.5$ is the null); dot, $q \leq 0.05$ with AUC above $0.5$. Programmes are identified only up to rotation, so columns are compared within a section by the recurrence of their labels, not as matched axes.\relax }}{24}{figure.caption.53}\protected@file@percent }
