\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S18}{\ignorespaces The diagnostics across the spill-over sweep, per fitted section: held-out reconstruction (nats per count), NMI of $\mathbf  {z}$ with the type, mirror $R^2$, cycle $R^2$ of $\mathbf  {z}$ and of $\mathbf  {w}$ on the top-decile cycling set, and the response's information about the niche beyond its within-type floor (nats). Line: mean over three seeds; band: their range. Each panel has its own vertical scale. The vertical line marks the operating point $\kappa = 0.1$, whose fits are the final fits. Column heads name the quantity on the axes below them. The cycle $R^2$ of $\mathbf  {w}$ is expected near zero (dashed). These readouts move with $\kappa $ by construction: a larger $\kappa $ assigns more of the neighbours' resemblance to spill-over, so the response's information about the niche and its spread fall, and the reconstruction favours small $\kappa $. The spill-over fraction $\kappa $ is not identified and is not selected on them; $\kappa = 0.1$ is the working point because it matches the typical per-cell misassignment \citep  {yang2025mistic}, not because of these curves. The values are in \cref  {tab:kappa-sweep}.\relax }}{33}{figure.caption.87}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:kappa-sweep}{{S18}{33}{The diagnostics across the spill-over sweep, per fitted section: held-out reconstruction (nats per count), NMI of $\vz $ with the type, mirror $R^2$, cycle $R^2$ of $\vz $ and of $\vw $ on the top-decile cycling set, and the response's information about the niche beyond its within-type floor (nats). Line: mean over three seeds; band: their range. Each panel has its own vertical scale. The vertical line marks the operating point $\kappa = 0.1$, whose fits are the final fits. Column heads name the quantity on the axes below them. The cycle $R^2$ of $\vw $ is expected near zero (dashed). These readouts move with $\kappa $ by construction: a larger $\kappa $ assigns more of the neighbours' resemblance to spill-over, so the response's information about the niche and its spread fall, and the reconstruction favours small $\kappa $. The spill-over fraction $\kappa $ is not identified and is not selected on them; $\kappa = 0.1$ is the working point because it matches the typical per-cell misassignment \citep {yang2025mistic}, not because of these curves. The values are in \cref {tab:kappa-sweep}.\relax }{figure.caption.87}{}}
\newlabel{fig:kappa-sweep@cref}{{[figure][18][]S18}{[1][33][]33}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The claimed contrasts and the rules.}{33}{section*.89}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S19}{\ignorespaces The claimed contrasts across the spill-over sweep, the measured counterpart of \cref  {fig:breakdown}. Rows: contrasts; columns: sections, with $m$ the number of contrasts in the section's set. At each $\kappa $, the mean over three seeds and its interval (spatial block bootstrap over tiles, two-sided, Bonferroni-adjusted over the section's $m$ contrasts); dashed, zero. Filled: the contrast holds at that grid point (every seed has the sign it has at $\kappa = 0$ and the interval excludes zero); hollow: from the breakdown point $\kappa ^\star $ on (dotted). Each panel has its own vertical scale, which always includes zero, so an interval far from zero can be shorter than its marker. Every contrast is signed so that it claims the side above zero. An empty panel: the contrast is not in that section's set. The margin over the programme part is not drawn: it is zero at $\kappa = 0$ by construction and is reported as a trajectory (\cref  {tab:breakdown-traj}). The breakdown points are listed in \cref  {tab:breakdown}.\relax }}{34}{figure.caption.90}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:breakdown-data}{{S19}{34}{The claimed contrasts across the spill-over sweep, the measured counterpart of \cref {fig:breakdown}. Rows: contrasts; columns: sections, with $m$ the number of contrasts in the section's set. At each $\kappa $, the mean over three seeds and its interval (spatial block bootstrap over tiles, two-sided, Bonferroni-adjusted over the section's $m$ contrasts); dashed, zero. Filled: the contrast holds at that grid point (every seed has the sign it has at $\kappa = 0$ and the interval excludes zero); hollow: from the breakdown point $\kappa ^\star $ on (dotted). Each panel has its own vertical scale, which always includes zero, so an interval far from zero can be shorter than its marker. Every contrast is signed so that it claims the side above zero. An empty panel: the contrast is not in that section's set. The margin over the programme part is not drawn: it is zero at $\kappa = 0$ by construction and is reported as a trajectory (\cref {tab:breakdown-traj}). The breakdown points are listed in \cref {tab:breakdown}.\relax }{figure.caption.90}{}}
\newlabel{fig:breakdown-data@cref}{{[figure][19][]S19}{[1][34][]34}}
